WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
Cut a tube straight across
and look at the slice:

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.840
you see a ring.

3
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.500
Cut the same tube along its length,
and you see two strips instead.

4
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.950
Same tube, two very different pictures.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.290
So when you cut open an
organ, or slice it thin,

6
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.550
how do you know what you are looking at?

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.430
In this mission, you'll
learn to dissect safely,

8
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.750
and why a sharp blade is
safer than a blunt one.

9
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.200
Then you'll orient a sheep's heart, using
the artery that runs diagonally across

10
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.350
its front.

11
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.600
Your mission: find out how to
identify what you find in an organ,

12
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.520
or in a thin slice of one.
